# Declaring the sample assets as binary stops Git from diffing, merging or
# line-ending-rewriting them.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.bmp  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary

# The sources keep their historical line endings instead of being normalised in
# the same commit that changes behaviour: a repository-wide renormalisation would
# turn every CRLF file into a whole-file diff. Until that separate pass happens,
# edit a file with the endings `git ls-files --eol` reports for it (see README).
